{
  "version": 1,
  "description": "Encrypted audit chain (spec §7). Entry i is an xc20p envelope with kid \"e<k>\" of cjson(event) under AuditKey[k] = HKDF-SHA256(ikm=VK[k], salt=b64decode(vault_id), info=utf8(\"akv1/audit-key\\n\") || cjson({key_epoch:k}), L=32), aad {ctx:\"akv1/audit\",vault_id,seq:i,prev,key_epoch:k}, prev = b64 sha256(cjson(entry i-1)) or \"\" for i=0. vault_keys: VK by epoch; each case lists the epochs the verifier holds (vault_key_epochs), the current membership key_epoch and min_key_epoch. The verifier MUST hold the key of key_epoch, and of every entry epoch >= min_key_epoch (else bad_request); min_key_epoch must lie in 1..key_epoch. Key epochs never decrease along the chain nor exceed key_epoch; an entry at an older epoch the verifier holds no key for is opaque ({seq,key_epoch,opaque:true}) but still hash-chained; a decrypted entry is {seq,key_epoch,opaque:false,event}. checkpoint {v,vault_id,seq,head,author,ts,sig} is signed with akv1/audit-checkpoint by a device of membership_events. cases MUST return `events` and `head`. event_envelopes (spec §7.1): the plaintext of an audit entry is {\"v\":1,\"type\",\"device_id\",\"ts\",...}; parseAuditEventEnvelope MUST return {type,device_id,ts} for each valid case and read no other field (an event of a type the reader does not know, such as rotation_started, is accepted on its envelope alone) and MUST fail invalid cases with expect_error. invalid MUST fail with expect_error (reorder/drop/substitution or a non-derived key -> decrypt_failed, truncation or rewritten tail vs witnessed checkpoint -> rollback, nonce reuse, non-epoch kid, decreasing or future epoch -> bad_request).",
